<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dost Mohammad Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1793">1793</a>–<a href="/years/1863">1863</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dost Mohammad Khan was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barakzai-dynasty">Barakzai dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>. He took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> in 1826 and assumed the title of emir in 1834. Deposed by a British invasion in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-afghan-war">First Anglo-Afghan War</a> in 1839, he was restored in 1842. He later brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandahar">Kandahar</a> under his rule in 1855 and captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herat">Herat</a> in 1863 after a ten-month siege, dying there days later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dost-mohammad-khan.jpg" alt="Dost Mohammad Khan" width="320" height="465" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: British Company artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dost_Mohammad_Khan_of_Afghanistan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
